Z||000002||Formula88||10-24-2001||10:01 AM||||To the best of my knowledge, it's a flat black, or semi-gloss at most.  I just repainted the vents on my Formula with DupliColor "Black" 1000* High Heat Engine Paint (note, the color is simply, Black, not flat black or gloss black).  They turned out very close to the vents on LZeitgeist's 60,000 mile original Formula.  His may have some fading on it, but overall it's very original and I've found it a great resource for how things should look.  LZ is a stickler for originality (3x trophey winning car - it's understandable) and he's going to use the same paint when he re-paints his vents.<P>I also used this same engine enamel on the sail panel frames and it also looks very close to factory (as close as I can tell with the naked eye, and not having an NOS part to comapare against).||||reg||4
