Z||000005||Formula88||10-24-2001||01:45 PM||||I don't think it's ceramic.  But the label did say 1000*F High Heat Engine paint.  It's a silver can with gold at the top, and a black cap (of course).  I got it at Wal Mart.  Shouldn't be too hard to find.||||reg||1
Z||000006||GodSend||10-24-2001||01:45 PM||||I have always wanted to chrome my deck grills.  I think that with a matching chrome intake on the side would look really nice.<P>I also have this wild fantasy of chroming the front lights.  Not the top part, but the black plastic pieces that cover the actual housing. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||skitime||10-24-2001||02:01 PM||||I could be wrong and hopefully CoolBlue87 will correct me if I am.  CoolBlue pointed out to me in Carlisle show that most people incorrectly think the engine covers are flat black.  His car only has 1700 miles and the were a gloss black.  We got to remember all of our cars are at least 13 years old so the black has faded and since everyones look the same we think that is normal.  <P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||LZeitgeist||10-24-2001||02:24 PM||||The thing I like so much about the High Heat paint is that it's durable, it doesn't usually need primer, and it's sort of a satin finish that leans ever so gently towards a very slight gloss. (The flatter the finish, the easier it is to make it lok professional out of a rattlecan. The glossier the finish, the harder it is to get a professional look.)<P>Oh, and thanks for the props, Formula88... but I have to say that the job he just did on his sail panel frames makes me jealous as Hell. My car is needing some attention here and there now that the show season's over, so I have a feeling that this coming year *his* 'twin' will be taking trophies away from my 'twin'. 8)<P><P>------------------<BR>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>1988 Red Fiero Formula<BR>- 1st Place - Stock Coupe - FOCOSEVA 2000<BR>- 3rd Place - Stock Formula - FOCOA Nat'l 2001<BR>- Class Winner - 1982 to Present - 2001 Tarheel Tigers All-Pontiac Show||||reg||1
Z||000009||Mark||10-24-2001||05:24 PM||||Krylon semi-flat black.  Really great stuff!||||reg||1
Z||000010||Phil||10-24-2001||06:44 PM||||Mar-Hyde  trim black  even has a Fiero on the can||||reg||1
