Z||000029||Formula88||10-29-2001||02:40 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by David DeVoe:<BR><B>Thanks for the info Formula, I see if I can find some of that paint. That wouldn't be duplcolors high heat ceramic paint would it? If it is I know that Auto Zone carries it.<BR>Thanks again<BR>Dave</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, I just went and got some more to do my new engine vents with.  Yes, it is the Duplicolor High Heat Ceramic 1000* Engine Paint.  The color is "Black" not semi-gloss or flat-black.  It has a bit of a satin finish that looks pretty good.  I also used it on my sail panel frames and it worked quite well.  Very closely matches the other trim on the car.<P>||||reg||1
